MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset="utf-8"
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Hello,

I am quite new with Shiny, but I stumbled onto a conflict between withMathJax and slider creations in the same renderUI.
Using the p function instead of withMathJax can overcome the issue, but it will not compile the LaTeX code.

I put below a minimal code for a reproducible example:

In the server.R:
library(shiny)
library(shinydashboard)
shinyServer(function(input, output) {
  reg<-reactive({
    column(width = 12,
           sliderInput(inputId = "exclu",
                       label = "Exlure les ... premières valeurs de la régression",
                       min = 0,max = 10,step = 1,value =1
           ),
           withMathJax("Be: $$ln(N_{(t)})=ln(k)+ln(2)\\times \\frac{t}{G}$$") ### replacing this by p("...") corrects the issue
    )
  })
  output$regression<-renderUI(reg())
}
)

The ui.R file:
library(shiny)

library(shinydashboard)
dashboardPage(
  dashboardHeader(title = "Generation time"),
  dashboardSidebar( sidebarMenu(
    menuItem("Graphic", tabName = "dashboard", icon = icon("dashboard"))
  )),
  dashboardBody(tabItem(tabName = "dashboard",
                              fluidRow(column(width = 6,offset = 0,
                                              h1("Parameters"),
                                              uiOutput("regression") ,
                                              align = "center"

                              )
                              )
  )
  )
)

Do you have any idea of what could trigger the issue? Is it some kind of conflict between the two functions to render the html page?

Thanks a lot,
Paul

